2f417bb2cba4f7ab5b61595cb6a499ce4b3d6cf2ff046a51adb1dfb","file":"preprints/A-power-saving-for-square-difference-free-sets-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":15,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"247b115928b9c6852e88ce723025093a391f6b67097db755bdb78252ebe02cd6","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-power-saving-for-square-difference-free-sets-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:9aac8a0642f417bb2cba4f7ab5b61595cb6a499ce4b3d6cf2ff046a51adb1dfb","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-power-saving-for-square-difference-free-sets-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L15"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere are absolute constants $c>0$ and $C<\\infty$ such that, for every\ninteger $N\\ge1$ and every square-difference-free set $A\\subseteq[N]$,\n\\[\n |A|\\le C N^{1-c}.\n\\]\nEquivalently, every subset of $[N]$ larger than $C N^{1-c}$ contains\ndistinct elements whose absolute difference is the square of a positive\ninteger."}
